Planning Commission
Minutes of the Proceedings - Final
August 8, 2024
Vice Chairman Watkins opened the Public Hearing. Hearing no comments the
hearing was closed and a motion and discussion called for.
Natacha Gaspar moved, seconded by Mark Smith to recommend approval
of the Subdivision Permit and Plat for Deer Valley at Chalk Bluff
Subdivision to the Laramie County Board of Commissioners and adopt the
findings of facts a and b of the staff report.
Watkins, Gaspar, Smith
Aye:
Caughey, Stadel
Excused:
3.
PUBLIC HEARING regarding a Subdivision Permit and Plat for
Allison Tracts, 11th Filing.
24 - 415
PZ-23-00109 PC Meeting Packet 8.8.24
Attachments:
Cate Cundall, Associate Planner, said that Steil Surveying Services, LLC, on behalf of
Everyday Homes, LLC, submitted a Subdivision Permit and Plat application for
Allison Tracts, 11th Filing, located in Tract 2, Allison Tracts, 10th Filing. This is a 1.7
acre vacant residential parcel that will be divided into a 7 tract subdivision, six will be
tiny home tracts and 1 a common space tract. The property is zoned MR-Medium
Density Residential. Water and sanitary sewer will be provided by South Cheyenne
Water and Sewer District. Access will be off East Allison Road.
Shane Hansen, agent for the applicant, was present to answer any questions.
Vice Chairman Watkins opened the Public Hearing. Receiving no comments the
hearing was closed and a motion was called for.
Mark Smith moved, seconded by Natacha Gaspar to recommend approval
of the Subdivision Permit and Plat for Allison Tracts, 11th Filing to the
Laramie County Board of Commissioners with no conditions and to adopt
the findings of fact a and b of the staff report. Vote 3-0.
Watkins, Gaspar, Smith
Aye:
Caughey, Stadel
Excused:
Adjournment
There being no further business Vice Chairman Watkins adjourned the meeting at 3:44 p.m.
CERTIFICATION
True and correct copy of the Minutes of the Proceedings for Thursday, August 8,
2024.
Approved by the Laramie County Planning Commission on Thursday, August 22,
2024.
